\section{Data Associations \& Constraints}
The system architecture is governed by the following relational constraints to ensure data consistency.

\begin{table}[h]
    \centering\small
    \begin{tabularx}{\linewidth}{@{} l c l L @{}}
        \toprule
        \textbf{Primary Entity} & \textbf{Cardinality} & \textbf{Related Entity} & \textbf{Logic \& Constraint} \\
        \midrule
        User & 1 : 1 & UserSettings & Profile-specific AI persona settings. \\
        User & 1 : 1 & WidgetLayouts & Serialized grid state of the React dashboard. \\
        User & 1 : N & Todo & Cascade delete: tasks are removed on account closure. \\
        User & 1 : N & Diary & Indexed by date for rapid calendar retrieval. \\
        ApiCache & 1 : 1 & Weather/Stock & Keyed by geolocation or ticker symbol. \\
        \bottomrule
    \end{tabularx}
\end{table}

\section{Detailed Entity Analysis}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.5em, labelsep=0.5em]
    \item \textbf{UserSettings.vis (JSONB)}: Utilizes native PostgreSQL JSON support for schema-less flexibility in widget state management.
    \item \textbf{Todo.is\_fixed (Boolean)}: Distinguishes recurring daily routines from one-time tasks, managed by the nightly reset worker.
    \item \textbf{BriefingWidget (Aggregate)}: A logical hub that prepares prompts for the Groq LLM by synthesizing rows from multiple tables.
\end{itemize}

\section{Front-end Implementation Plan}
The UI is a single-page application built with \textbf{React.js} and \textbf{Tailwind CSS}.

\textbf{Component Architecture}
\begin{itemize}[noitemsep]
    \item \textbf{Grid System}: \texttt{react-grid-layout} is used for draggable widgets, with positions persisted in \texttt{WidgetLayouts}.
    \item \textbf{Theming}: Dynamic CSS variables are mapped to the AI Persona selected in \texttt{UserSettings}.
    \item \textbf{State Management}: React hooks synchronize cached API data with the view to minimize re-renders.
\end{itemize}

